cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |
  If you use this benchmark or build on the eval-gated self-evolution
  methodology in academic work, please cite the companion technical
  report (see README "Citation" section) and acknowledge the
  eval-gated self-evolution framework.
title: "WSE-Bench — Eval-Gated Self-Evolution Benchmark"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-26
license: MIT
type: dataset
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - llm-evaluation
  - self-evolution
  - eval-gated
  - mcnemar-test
  - reproducible-research
abstract: |
  WSE-Bench is a 156-task reading-comprehension + reasoning + citation
  verification benchmark designed to evaluate **eval-gated self-evolution**
  loops on small LLMs. Each task is graded by a deterministic rubric and
  admits paired McNemar testing across candidate vs. baseline system
  prompts. The benchmark ships with a per-round evolution ledger, an
  auditing toolkit for measurement-validity defects, and a generation
  harness that uses 4-bit Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct under a fixed sampling
  protocol (temperature=0.7, top_p=0.9, max_new_tokens=128,
  repetition_penalty=1.05, do_sample=True).
url: "https://github.com/aidless/wse-bench-public"
